// It returns a Vec<char> satisfying these constraints.
//
// Idea:
// Using only two characters 'a' and 'b', the condition seq[i] != seq[i+2]
// means the sequence must alternate every two steps. That means positions
// with the same parity must have different characters. But since we only use
// 'a' and 'b', the simplest sequence is just alternating 'a' and 'b':
